    "text": "Long-Horizon-Terminal-Bench includes 46 long-horizon tasks across nine categories.",
    "topic": "Long-Horizon-Task Categories"
  },
  {
    "text": "The benchmark evaluates agents on five dimensions: generalization, memory, precision, long-horizon execution, and open-vocabulary instruction following.",
    "topic": "Benchmark Evaluation Dimensions"
  },
  {
    "text": "WorldLines tasks are designed to couple long-term memory translation with partial observability and state overwrite.",
    "topic": "WorldLines Task Design"
  },
  {
    "text": "A direct empirical comparison between reactive implicit-memory policies and explicit memory-to-plan systems on shared long-horizon tasks is proposed to assess the necessity of explicit translation.",
    "topic": "Empirical Comparison Proposal"
  },
  {
    "text": "Long-Short-Term-Memory-Bench is a terminal benchmark focused on long-horizon tasks with dense reward-based grading.",
